Description: Stereo 3D for Direct3D 9 games on Wine and Proton, full side by side
 wiz3D, the stereo wrapper from the iZ3D driver, renders a Direct3D 9 game
 once per eye and hands KWin one format: full side by side, left eye first,
 declared on the game window. KWin shows it in whatever stereo output the
 screen uses.
 .
 The package ships the Windows proxy DLLs for 64-bit (/usr/lib/wiz3d/x64) and
 32-bit (/usr/lib/wiz3d/x86) games, wiz3d-run, the launcher that declares
 the window, and wiz3d-launch, which makes a game's Wine prefix when it does
 not exist (DXVK, Microsoft's d3dx9 through winetricks, the user folders
 inside the prefix), puts wiz3D in it in front of DXVK, runs the game in its
 own folder and takes wiz3D out again. For Steam, use "wiz3d-run -- %command%"
 as the launch option with the matching tree copied into the game's folder.
